// Example of machine-local key bindings for a Mac.
//
// Copy it, as keybindings.json, into the machine-local directory that
// `bin/vscode-settings status` prints, and remove the comment marks of the lines you
// need. Its rules come after those of user/keybindings.json, so they win.
// Untested: derived from the keymaps of VS Code and of the extensions, never pressed on a Mac.
[
  // On a Mac, Option types characters, and a rule on alt+KEY takes the character away. The
  // key check of the first-day tutorial tells which lines to enable.

  // French keyboard: Option+Shift+( types [
  // { "key": "alt+shift+5", "command": "-emacs-mcx.queryReplace" },
  // French keyboard: Option+Shift+: types a backslash
  // { "key": "alt+/", "command": "-editor.action.triggerSuggest" },
  // Any keyboard: Option+C types a c with a cedilla again, instead of capitalising a word
  // { "key": "alt+c", "command": "-emacs-mcx.transformToTitlecase" },
]
